{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nq=[i for i in s['investigations'] if i['id'].startswith('6491640e')][0]\nks=[x['id'] for x in s['knowledge'] if x['id'].startswith('6491640e')]\nsrc=['raft_append_config','raft_dispatch_logs','raft_setup_leader_state','raft_quorum_size2','raft_elect_self','api_remove_server','cfg_next_configuration']\ninterp={\n 'investigation_id':q['id'],\n 'experiment_id':'6491640ed49a4c7b8f5150438d350e36-experiment',\n 'source_ids':src,\n 'executions':{'0e6dd623c01e43a4b9e33cafc544ecf2':[0,1]},\n 'conclusion':'violated',\n 'defect_claim':'asserted',\n 'rationale':(\\\"Conclusion: violated, and the scoped defect is asserted. A configuration change whose log write fails is reported to the caller as failed, but the \\\"\n   \\\"new configuration is nevertheless installed in the leader's in-memory latest configuration at the index the entry would have occupied. The node then \\\"\n   \\\"treats that unstored configuration as authoritative: it re-elects itself with the shrunken voter set and reports a client command committed with only its own \\\"\n   \\\"acknowledgement, while the other member of the committed configuration does not have that entry. Evidence from receipt 0e6dd623c01e43a4b9e33cafc544ecf2 \\\"\n   \\\"(completed, tests_passed, exit 0). Parsed index 0, the case event: two voters were bootstrapped, the leader's store failed exactly the configuration write, \\\"\n   \\\"and afterwards latest_index_after_fail=3 with last_log_index_after_fail=2, while phantom_servers records the shrunken configuration containing only the \\\"\n   \\\"leader itself. Parsed index 1, the result: remove_failed=true with remove_error 'injected store failure', latest_index_exceeds_log=true, re_elected=true, \\\"\n   \\\"apply_ok=true, commit_index=4, leader_last_index=4 and peer_last_index=2, so commit_without_peer=true. Under the committed two-voter configuration a quorum \\\"\n   \\\"is both members, so the command the client was told had committed at index 4 never reached a quorum of that configuration. Mechanism from source: \\\"\n   \\\"appendConfigurationEntry dispatches the configuration entry and then, unconditionally, calls setLatestConfiguration with the new configuration at the \\\"\n   \\\"dispatched index, reconfigures the commitment map and restarts replication (raft.go:1204-1244), while dispatchLogs' store-error path only answers the futures \\\"\n   \\\"with the error and moves the node to follower (raft.go:1245-1296). quorumSize, electSelf and setupLeaderState all read that latest configuration \\\"\n   \\\"(raft.go:1087-1100, 1999-2071, 456-468), so the phantom configuration governs both the election the node wins alone and the quorum it uses to commit. \\\"\n   \\\"Consequence under the exercised conditions: after a transient failure to store a configuration change, the leader can adopt a voter set that the rest of the \\\"\n   \\\"cluster never accepted and serve client commits that no quorum of the committed configuration holds.\\\"),\n 'counterevidence':[\n  \\\"The phantom configuration exists only in memory: a restart rebuilds configurations from the log, so the effect is bounded by the node's uptime unless a later successful configuration write extends it, and the harness did not restart the node.\\\",\n  \\\"The commit without a peer required the store to fail once and then succeed: the harness fails a single StoreLogs call, and a persistent write failure would also block the later client command, so the exercised trigger is a transient store error rather than a permanent one.\\\",\n  \\\"The other voter never accepted the phantom configuration and still holds the committed two-voter view, so its own elections fail while the phantom leader lives; the harness observed the leader's side only and did not measure how long the peer stays unable to win.\\\",\n  \\\"No data was corrupted: the client command was applied to the phantom leader's own state machine, and the failure mode is a commit reported without a quorum of the committed configuration.\\\"\n ],\n 'limitations':[\n  \\\"One configuration shape (two voters), one injected failure and one run; no repetition, no three-member cluster and no non-voter in the configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"The harness applies its command immediately after the node returns to Leader and does not test whether a later successful configuration change repairs or compounds the phantom view.\\\",\n  \\\"Restart behaviour, which is where the log-derived configuration would replace the phantom one, was not exercised, so nothing is claimed about recovery from this state.\\\",\n  \\\"The client-visible completion point was the Apply future returning nil; no read path through the FSM was exercised.\\\"\n ],\n 'knowledge':[{'entry_id':ks[0],'revision':1,'assertion':'appendConfigurationEntry installs the new configuration in memory regardless of whether its log entry was stored.'},\n              {'entry_id':ks[1],'revision':1,'assertion':'quorumSize, electSelf and setupLeaderState derive voter sets from the latest configuration.'}]\n}\njson.dump({'rationale':(\\\"Interpret the phantom-configuration execution: the failed RemoveServer was reported as failed yet left the leader holding a configuration at an \\\"\n  \\\"index beyond its log, after which it re-elected itself and committed a client command at index 4 while the other voter held index 2. The question is recorded \\\"\n  \\\"as violated with the safety defect asserted, and the transient-failure premise, memory-only lifetime, unmeasured peer liveness and untested restart are kept as \\\"\n  \\\"counterevidence and limits.\\\"),\n 'interpretations':[interp]},open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
